EXPERIMENT 10: Address of Variables and Virtual Memory

Theory:
- &: Gives the memory address of a variable.
- Virtual Address Space: When multiple instances of a program run simultaneously, each process has its own isolated virtual memory address space. These map to physical RAM locations.
- while(1): An infinite loop that keeps the process running in the background.
- sleep(1): Pauses program execution for one second.
- int var = 42: Declares and initializes a local integer variable stored on the process's stack memory.
- fflush(stdout): Flushes the output stream so that text prints to the terminal immediately.
